        "mission_intent": "Subject: Full Specification for Updated Incident Handling Reporting Framework\n\nTeam, we need to build out a comprehensive security operations reporting specification aligned with the NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 2 Computer Security Incident Handling Guide. The framework should cover the full incident response lifecycle\u2014preparation, detection and analysis, containment/eradication/recovery, and post-incident activity\u2014with reporting templates and escalation procedures for each phase. Please ensure the spec includes integration points for coordination with US-CERT, relevant ISACs (including REN-ISAC), and sector-specific partners such as DOE, State, FAA, and CDC, reflecting the multi-agency coordination model described in the guide. Reporting outputs should capture indicators of compromise, incident categorization and prioritization criteria, impact assessments, and lessons-learned summaries. The specification must define data-sharing formats compatible with federal reporting requirements and address handling markings (TLP or equivalent) for all shared artifacts. We need role-based access controls for report consumers, retention policies consistent with federal records management, and automated notification triggers for severity escalations. Draft the full specification by end of next quarter, with an interim review milestone at the six-week mark so we can validate alignment with our SOC's existing SIEM and ticketing platforms before finalizing.",
